// Change: new rule
// Title: Windows Update Disabled Via Registry
// Sigma ID: 1bff5de9-819d-41f3-90cd-b4dae2443bef
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-08-14 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects registry modifications that disable Windows Update automatic updates or block access to
//   the Windows Update service entirely. Malware and ransomware commonly disable Windows Update to
//   prevent security patches from being applied and to stop update-triggered reboots that could
//   interfere with their operation.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate disabling of Windows Update via Group Policy or other administrative tools
// References:
//   - https://github.com/jebofponderworthy/windows-tools/blob/d43204b11e47163f842b5a4ffd76163f27ef69e2/incoming/Enable-Windows-Update-Using-Registry.ps1
//   - https://github.com/jebofponderworthy/windows-tools/blob/7039ad4326793ff3e6935e1ee8bdd3694cb71793/tools/update-windows-with-reboot.ps1
//   - https://github.com/Siradankullanici/OpenSourceViruses/blob/3267564a35f6e13559a3119eb68d0da8d2e91a0a/suspiciousregchangesandtaskkils
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/e6fa05ce10d4092a1de7d7380da240a34a30b555/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_disable_windows_update.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey contains "\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WindowsUpdate" or RegistryKey contains "\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Explorer" or RegistryKey contains "\\SYSTEM\\Internet Communication Management\\Internet Communication") and (RegistryKey endswith "\\AU\\NoAutoUpdate" or RegistryKey endswith "\\DisableWindowsUpdateAccess") and RegistryValueData =~ "DWORD (0x00000001)"
